= Research Question

I explored whether a nonequilibrium fluctuation-theorem framework developed for surface temperature could be extended to total column water vapor (TCWV) and precipitation.

= Approach and Findings

Using ERA5, I compared probability-density-function asymmetry across 5-, 10-, 15-, and 20-year smoothing windows and examined the relationship between SST and TCWV. The draft reports an SST–TCWV regression slope of 0.0645 K⁻¹ ($R^2 = 0.95$), close to Clausius–Clapeyron scaling. I also explored positive and negative distribution tails and the joint relationship of TCWV and vertical motion with precipitation.

= Outcome

I produced analysis code, figures, and manuscript drafts in Typst and LaTeX, and discussed the interpretation with #link("https://www.polito.it/en/staff?p=lamberto.rondoni")[Prof. Lamberto Rondoni]. I stopped this direction at the draft stage after encountering difficulties with originality and the theoretical basis of the proposed relationship.
